Source: rustls-ffi-quic
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
# cargo, rustc and cargo-c are not listed: this is built with the builder's own rustup toolchain (see build.sh),
# which dpkg's dependency check cannot see.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               pkgconf,
Standards-Version: 4.7.3
Homepage: https://github.com/small-gear-lab/rustls-ffi-quic
Rules-Requires-Root: no

# The soname is librustls_quic.so.<upstream version>: every release is its own soname, so the package is named after
# it. build.sh replaces @SOVER@ by the version of rustls-ffi this is based on.
Package: librustls-quic@SOVER@
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: C bindings for the Rustls TLS library, with a QUIC API
 rustls-ffi-quic is rustls-ffi, the C bindings of Rustls, with a C API over
 rustls::quic added, so that a QUIC stack (ngtcp2, for curl's HTTP/3) can use
 Rustls for the TLS part of the handshake.
 .
 The exported functions are named rustlsq_*, not rustls_*, so that this library
 can be loaded in the same process as rustls-ffi (librustls) without the two
 answering for each other.
 .
 This build uses the aws-lc-rs crypto provider, which has the HPKE support
 that Encrypted Client Hello needs, and enables certificate compression
 (brotli and zlib).

Package: librustls-quic-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: librustls-quic@SOVER@ (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: C bindings for the Rustls TLS library, with a QUIC API (development files)
 rustls-ffi-quic is rustls-ffi with a C API over rustls::quic added.
 .
 This package provides the headers (rustls-quic/rustls.h, which also maps the
 names rustls-ffi has to the rustlsq_* ones through
 rustls-quic/rustls_upstream_names.h), the librustls_quic.so link and the
 rustls-quic.pc file for pkg-config. There is no static library: it is 40 MB
 and nothing here needs it.
